\par
\b 13. Kubernetes Deployment Verification\b0\par
Run locally or from the self-hosted runner:\par
\f1 kubectl config current-context\par
kubectl get nodes\par
kubectl get deployments,pods,services -n taskflow\par
\f0\par
Expected backend state:\par
\f1 user-service: 3/3\par
task-service: 3/3\par
stats-service: 3/3\par
frontend: 1/1\par
\f0\par
Take Screenshot 5: Kubernetes rollout and Pods.\par
\par
\b 14. Health Check Verification\b0\par
\f1 kubectl exec -n taskflow deployment/user-service -- wget -qO- http://localhost:4001/health\par
kubectl exec -n taskflow deployment/task-service -- wget -qO- http://localhost:4002/health\par
kubectl exec -n taskflow deployment/stats-service -- wget -qO- http://localhost:4003/health\par
\f0\par
Take Screenshot 6: Successful post-deployment health checks.\par
\par
\b 15. Rollback\b0\par
View rollout history:\par
\f1 kubectl rollout history deployment/task-service -n taskflow\par
\f0\par
Rollback the last release:\par
\f1 kubectl rollout undo deployment/task-service -n taskflow\par
kubectl rollout status deployment/task-service -n taskflow\par
\f0\par
Take Screenshot 7: Rollback completed successfully.\par
\par
\b 16. Deployment Strategies\b0\par
The current pipeline uses a rolling update. Kubernetes gradually replaces old Pods with new Pods and keeps the Service available when readiness probes pass.\par
\par
\b 17. Troubleshooting\b0\par
\tab Docker login failure: check \f1 DOCKERHUB_USERNAME\f0 and \f1 DOCKERHUB_TOKEN\f0 .\par
\tab ImagePullBackOff: verify that the Docker Hub repositories are public or configure image pull credentials.\par
\tab Self-hosted runner unavailable: verify the runner is online and has the \f1 self-hosted\f0 label.\par
\tab Kubernetes context failure: run \f1 kubectl config current-context\f0 on the runner.\par
\tab Failed health check: inspect \f1 kubectl logs\f0 and \f1 kubectl describe pod\f0 .\par
\par
\b 18. Result\b0\par
The CI/CD workflow validates the application, builds four Docker images, publishes immutable and latest tags to Docker Hub, and provides a controlled manual deployment stage for Kubernetes. Rollout status and health checks verify the deployment.\par
\par
\b 19. Conclusion\b0\par
CI/CD automates the path from a GitHub commit to a tested Docker image and a Kubernetes release. It improves repeatability, reduces manual errors, and supports rollback when a deployment is unsuccessful.\par
